From 8bed95f96965b724aa42108e0a38e0c6e5c34e7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: onlyfish <linotfish@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:28:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] audioflinger: keep the DAP controller lock off the HAL query
 and the mixer

EffectDapController::mLock was held across AudioFlinger::getParameters()
(AudioFlinger_Mutex + hardwareMutex + HAL IPC) in onUpmixPlayingPkg(),
onSomcPrioritizedApps() and onSomcExcludedApps(), while the mixer thread took
mLock with ThreadBase_Mutex already held from prepareTracks_l(). A third thread
in AudioFlinger::releaseAudioSessionId() closed the cycle:

  mixer:          ThreadBase_Mutex -> mLock
  audio command:  mLock -> AudioFlinger_Mutex
  binder:         AudioFlinger_Mutex -> lockEffectChains_l -> ThreadBase_Mutex

audioserver then aborted with a TimeCheck timeout for
IAudioPolicyService::getStreamTypeForAttributes, because audio policy held
AudioPolicyService_Mutex while waiting for the audio command thread.

Resolve the upmix-supported-package state in two phases: update the snapshot and
run the list checks under mLock, then query the HAL and the package manager
outside it, and finally apply the result under the lock. mLock is a leaf lock
again.

Also make consumePendingMlVolumeResync() lock-free: it runs on the mixer thread
with ThreadBase_Mutex held, so it must never block on mLock. A pointer identity
token in an atomic is enough because the thread handle is only compared.

Change-Id: Id8b4fbd0450c0f185e6cfacd3fbcfc7759a3607d
---
 services/audioflinger/EffectDapController.cpp | 107 ++++++++++++------
 services/audioflinger/EffectDapController.h   |  10 +-
 2 files changed, 81 insertions(+), 36 deletions(-)

